0..76 Comment "// A hold at grade one. `var[1] c = e;` holds a value no one else holds: the"
77..154 Comment "// value is made where the hold stands, and it is never copied while held. An"
155..230 Comment "// exclusive access moves the value out to its view, the view is read once,"
231..309 Comment "// and `resume` writes the new value back, so the write-back needs no count of"
310..387 Comment "// the value\'s other holders. `var c = e;` holds at the default grade ω, and"
388..451 Comment "// each read of it copies. The grades are those of graded modal"
452..526 Comment "// types (Orchard, Liepelt and Eades, \"Quantitative program reasoning with"
527..562 Comment "// graded modal types\", ICFP 2019)."
564..639 Comment "// The successor, a call whose type synthesises where a statement binds it."
640..646 Keyword "import"
